WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.794
- I had somebody ask me
if I caught the PTSD

00:00:02.794 --> 00:00:06.715
like the flu, did I what,
did I catch the PTSD?

00:00:10.593 --> 00:00:11.678
- There's no way that the military

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:14.264
has females on the front
line, there's no way

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:19.144
that you as small as you are
were able to shoot a 50 cal.

00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:23.940
No, I did every day all day
and was pretty good at it too.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:27.736
- When I'm wearing my
little pink USMC veteran hat

00:00:27.736 --> 00:00:30.905
and someone says so how did you serve.

00:00:30.905 --> 00:00:32.782
I was like well I was a marine, oh wow,

00:00:32.782 --> 00:00:35.201
you don't look like a Marine.

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:39.247
- A veteran is someone who
served, a veteran looks like me.

00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:42.751
- Humor is one way of just coping

00:00:42.751 --> 00:00:45.837
with stress, it's a release.

00:00:45.837 --> 00:00:48.923
- I got this backpack
and inside this backpack

00:00:48.923 --> 00:00:50.300
a couple pairs of T-shirts, a couple pair

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:54.804
of shorts, couple pairs
of underwear some socks.

00:00:54.804 --> 00:00:58.808
Which luckily now last me
twice as long as you folks.

00:00:58.808 --> 00:00:59.934
It's okay to laugh if the one-legged

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:02.687
dude is telling the one-legged jokes.

00:01:02.687 --> 00:01:04.564
- Shaving one eyebrow off while the

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:06.441
other soldiers asleep and he wakes up only

00:01:06.441 --> 00:01:08.109
have one eyebrow, that was humor.

00:01:08.109 --> 00:01:11.946
- If you can laugh about
things, then you can take away

00:01:11.946 --> 00:01:13.948
some of the seriousness that's there.

00:01:13.948 --> 00:01:16.451
- There's a such thing
as invisible wounds.

00:01:16.451 --> 00:01:17.994
They don't see me as a disabled

00:01:17.994 --> 00:01:20.955
veteran because I have all my limbs.

00:01:20.955 --> 00:01:23.083
- Traumatic brain injury,
post traumatic stress,

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:25.585
whatever that might be,
and you can't see them.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:28.963
They look fully functioning
but they're severely injured.

00:01:28.963 --> 00:01:32.342
- Post traumatic stress is an isolator.

00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:34.344
- Post traumatic stress
it's kinda stigmatized.

00:01:34.344 --> 00:01:37.263
It isn't something
that just happens in war.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.681
It's something that happens when you

00:01:38.681 --> 00:01:42.727
get put in an extreme circumstance,
it's a human experience.

00:01:42.727 --> 00:01:43.895
- The biggest thing that people think

00:01:43.895 --> 00:01:47.440
is that we're all angry, that we're always

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.360
mad about something or that you can't

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:53.738
ask us a question because we'll freak out.

00:01:53.738 --> 00:01:55.573
- You end up living with that for a

00:01:55.573 --> 00:01:57.492
long time, that survivor's guilt.

00:01:57.492 --> 00:01:58.952
- What if, what if I'd just been paying

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.412
a little bit closer attention,
could I have seen something.

00:02:01.412 --> 00:02:02.789
They come up to you and
they shake your hand and

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.457
they thank you for your
service and they call

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:09.379
you a hero and you're like
heroes don't get people killed.

00:02:09.379 --> 00:02:11.422
- When I started talking to
the Wounded Warrior Project,

00:02:11.422 --> 00:02:14.676
it I say my life fell
apart, they kind of like

00:02:14.676 --> 00:02:17.846
gave me like the plans to figure out

00:02:17.846 --> 00:02:19.722
so I could put it back together.

00:02:19.722 --> 00:02:21.975
- 21, 22 veterans a day committing suicide

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:24.018
is just a little too much for me.

00:02:24.018 --> 00:02:25.478
And nobody should have to lose their life

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:28.982
from war after they've come home from war.

00:02:29.899 --> 00:02:32.152
There's a lot of people that feel alone.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:36.197
I need to step up and make
other people not feel alone.

